    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, so i'm currently on methylphenidate for my adhd, but i feel like i've hit a plateau with my focus. since finals are coming up, i've been reading about biohacking and stacking stimulants to maximize cognitive output. i'm thinking about adding about 400-600mg of caffeine via pills to my ritalin dose to really stay locked in for these all-nighters. do you think that's a good way to optimize my performance, or is that too much?",
